    <string name="section_about">About</string>
    <string name="about_version">FocusLock version %1$s</string>
    <string name="about_developer">Developed by ronny raj</string>
    <string name="about_email">funnypawan8@gmail.com</string>
    <string name="about_privacy">Privacy: FocusLock stores limits, usage summaries and emergency counters only on this device. It never uploads your limits or usage data, and collects no contacts, messages, location or screen content. Internet is used only to show ads via Google AdMob, which may use the device advertising ID to show ads. Accessibility data never leaves this device.\n\nHonest limits: FocusLock is a self-control tool, not a lock against the device owner. A determined owner can uninstall it, force-stop it, or revoke its permissions in Android Settings (FocusLock warns you when protection degrades). True tamper-proof control requires Android\'s managed-device / parental-control features (e.g. a supervised device), which FocusLock does not pretend to replace.</string>
    <string name="confirm_disable_protection_title">Turn off all protection?</string>
    <string name="confirm_disable_protection_msg">No app will be blocked until you turn protection back on. Your limits, statistics and emergency counters are kept.</string>

